(c4) O[O saving Victim, op'ning wide The gate of heav'n to man below,](g) sa(gh!jvIH)lu(gf)tá(hg)ris(hih) Hó(g')sti(f)a,(g.) (;)
Quae(g) cae(i')li(j) pan(k)dis(ji) ó(hg)sti(h)um,(j.) (:)
Bel[Our foes press on from ev'ry side Thine aid supply, thy strength bestow.](j)la(h') pre(j)munt(g) ho(gh)stí(hg)li(f)a,(g.) (;)
Da(f) ro(hg)bur,(hj) fer(ji) au(hg)xí(e')li(f)um.(g.) (::) (z)
2. U[To Thy great Name be endless praise, Immortal Godhead One in Three;](g)ni(gh!jvIH) tri(gf)nó(hg)que(hih) Dó(g')mi(f)no(g.) (;)
Sit(g) sem(i')pi(j)tér(k)na(ji) gló(hg)ri(h)a :(j.) (:) (z)
Qui[O grant us endless length of days In our true native land with Thee.](j) vi(h')tam(j) si(g)ne(gh) tér(hg)mi(f)no(g.) (;)
No(f)bis(hg) do(hj)net(ji) in(hg) pá(e')tri(f)a.(g.) (::) 
